WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.183
When a laptop plugs into a switch,

2
00:00:02.183 --> 00:00:05.500
the switch asks a RADIUS
server whether to let it on.

3
00:00:05.500 --> 00:00:10.875
Today that's usually NPS, and NPS
checks with AD, so it ends with AD.

4
00:00:10.875 --> 00:00:15.300
People expect Microsoft to offer
a RADIUS service in Entra ID.

5
00:00:15.300 --> 00:00:16.187
It doesn't.

6
00:00:16.187 --> 00:00:17.726
So there are four choices.

7
00:00:17.726 --> 00:00:19.600
Keep NPS as a bridge.

8
00:00:19.600 --> 00:00:23.500
Move to a network access control
platform that checks Intune,

9
00:00:23.500 --> 00:00:25.412
which is the program's default.

10
00:00:25.412 --> 00:00:29.688
A cloud RADIUS service, except
none is FedRAMP-authorized yet.

11
00:00:29.688 --> 00:00:32.722
Or, for remote users,
Global Secure Access,

12
00:00:32.722 --> 00:00:37.420
which replaces the VPN, but not
the switch on the campus network.
